    <string name="map_off_text">Latent does not use the internet unless you let it. To show where your photos were taken on a map, it has to download map pictures from OpenStreetMap. The map server learns which areas you look at, and your IP address; it is never sent your photos, their names or their places as a list.</string>
    <string name="map_turn_on">Turn on online maps</string>
    <string name="map_turn_off">Turn off online maps</string>
    <string name="map_ask_title">Use the internet for maps?</string>
    <string name="map_ask_text">Latent will download map pictures from OpenStreetMap while the map is open. Nothing else is sent. You can turn this off again from the map\'s menu.</string>
